import ../../helpers/driver.dl

window test controls:
    button "Go"
    switch "Motion"

set state to 0
set instance to an instance of test controls with state (the address of state)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 640 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set button to the UI layout for element (the control labeled "Go" in (the address of instance)) in (view's layout)
set view's cursor to a UI point at (button's painted bounds' x + 4.0) and (button's painted bounds' y + 4.0)
require condition (update UI view (the address of view)) reporting "Hover did not schedule its animation"
set index to 0
loop while view's animating:
    set view's seconds to view's seconds + 0.016
    ignore update UI view (the address of view)
    increment index
    require condition (index < 100) reporting "The hover animation never settled"
require condition (button's hover = 1.0) reporting "Hover did not reach its destination"
set count to view's paint count
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's paint count = count) reporting "Hover kept painting after it settled"
set view's cursor to a UI point at 0.0 and 0.0
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
loop while view's animating:
    set view's seconds to view's seconds + 0.016
    ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (button's hover = 0.0) reporting "Hover did not fade out"
set toggle to the UI layout for element (the control labeled "Motion" in (the address of instance)) in (view's layout)
set view's cursor to a UI point at (toggle's painted bounds' x + 4.0) and (toggle's painted bounds' y + 4.0)
set view's down to true
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set view's down to false
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (the "Motion" switch is on in (the address of instance)) reporting "The shared input handler did not activate the switch"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Shared hit testing works; hover frames stop when settled."
